<h2>Level 1 · Find exactly (CLAUDE.md as a router)</h2>
<p>Every Second Brain <strong>starts here</strong>. You need exactly two things &mdash; <strong>a single <code>CLAUDE.md</code></strong> and <strong>a few folders and files</strong>. The question at this level is simple. <strong>"That word or file I wrote &mdash; where is it?"</strong></p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">What CLAUDE.md is</span>
    It is a file that is <strong>read automatically</strong> when you open the project folder. It works like the <strong>system prompt</strong> for that session (see <a href="#!ccb-claudemd">CLAUDE.md instructions</a> for details). The key point here is using this file as a <strong>"router (a signpost)"</strong>.
</div>

<h3>CLAUDE.md = role introduction + routing rules</h3>
<p>In <code>CLAUDE.md</code> you write not only "who you are and what matters" but also <strong>"which information lives in which folder"</strong>. These are the <strong>routing rules</strong>.</p>
<pre><code><span class="c"># CLAUDE.md — example routing rules (signposts)</span>
- If you need personal info about me  → read context/about-me.md
- If you wonder about the stack/env   → read context/stack.md
- Q1 priorities for this year         → they are in projects/2026-q1.md
- Big decisions and their reasons     → context/decisions.md (decision log)</code></pre>

